  "native_executable_sha256": "9d4e651e820e18f331c7328f90500c941d4051552ab750b559f5190eb7902fe3",
  "diff": {
    "path": "docs/planning/reviews/C08/attempt-01/diff.patch",
    "sha256": "b803670c2f88aaeee454efbde4cb525d8c4b495d99a356b031697c85e1da38d1"
  },
  "limitations": [
    "D034 (decisions.md, AGENTS.md, review-protocol.md; owner rule 2026-10-18): chunk reviews complete at 8/10 in all five scores with no blockers (xtask complete --owner-accept, decision D034); phase reviews need 9/10 without owner acceptance, and every chunk accepted below 9 is raised to a passing review before its phase completes. crates/xtask/src/complete.rs enforces both (owner_accepted; test d034_phases_need_nine_and_every_eight_chunk_is_raised_before_sign_off). A stale controller expectation (P03's first member without an inventory) now names C09.",
    "D033 (decisions.md) and the DESIGN C08 section record the SDK `management` feature (scm-sdk =0.1.0 built from 4f65dc48, which contains the reviewed Phase4 commit 32cbcb6d; checked read-only with git merge-base; no version, checksum or lockfile change), the separate management credential class bound to its token origin, production-only default endpoints (custom management endpoints deferred; the fixture build reads a management origin file in its own data root), per-generation bindings and the redaction list. The DESIGN section carries the operation/option coverage map from v1's bridge operations.ts to SDK calls.",
    "No real management endpoint was called. Rust (tests/management_reads, 12 tests) and native acceptance use synthetic TLS endpoints: the Rust test server, and tools/native-acceptance/mgmt_server.py (token, AIRS management and DLP reads, form-encoded Basic client authentication as the SDK sends it) beside scan_server.py. Live management behavior is qualified in C25.",
    "Paging follows v1's bridge rules (pagination.total_items, next_offset with zero as none, required vs optional inventory arrays, Spring last/totalPages/totalElements) except that a full AIRS page without a cursor is not taken as the last page (v1 did); the next page is offered instead, so completeness is never claimed without the service's signal. DLP details use the SDK's own get (404 is absent) as v1 did; other details use v1's bounded walk (40 x 25) and report incomplete, never absent, when the walk ends before the inventory.",
    "The SDK's response contracts keep unknown enum values (Patch extensions) but reject structurally invalid DLP replies (for example a detection_config without its required technique); those are reported as invalid responses, never as absent (dlp_details_use_their_own_read_and_a_404_means_absent).",
    "Native acceptance found Administration's 'Next page' 12 px under the bottom fade at the minimum window size. Diagnosis (End key did not move the page): at exactly 900 CSS px the shared frame keeps its 32 px bottom padding under the 60 px fade, so a page's last control could never scroll clear. The shell's status line now adds bottom space (pb-14), and the focus-reveal handler also moves a focused page control inside the scroll-padded area on the next animation frame, after WebKit's own focus scroll (desktop-shell.tsx; desktop-shell.test.tsx; two mutation probes). Two earlier fix attempts failed natively and are not claimed. Because this touches the shell and Settings gained the management form, C01-C07 native acceptance were re-run as regressions on the C08 bundle (docs/planning/evidence/C08/native-acceptance-C0x.json and native-regressions/); the C01 driver now expects Administration available and the C02 driver walks 60 Tab stops.",
    "Administration's inventory picker is a group of buttons (aria-current marks the shown inventory) rather than a select, so it is fully keyboard and Accessibility operable; the filter applies to the current page only and says so. Runtime's scan profile remains an explicit typed name or ID; inventories never select one.",
    "Mutation probes: docs/planning/evidence/C08/mutation-probes (credential separation, token-origin binding, TSG requirement, class-scoped removal, retired-generation results, paging and completeness, total_items, required arrays, walk vs absent, DLP 404 mapping, recursive redaction, contract validation, partial/stale/empty UI states, superseded replies, local-preview classification, secret field clearing and the focus-reveal correction; baselines pass; run in a disposable copy)."
  ],
